{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790192138,"nonce":"NEwMyL8ohyi7LZvPncJPDBZN9nY=","message":"Revised 2026-09-23 (Luis): `tui` is not a command. This task is the terminal renderer of view specs, sitting behind `git work view \u003ckind\u003e` and `git work flow run \u003cname\u003e` when stdout is a TTY. It implements the view kinds (list, board, gantt) against the spec that `view.*` builds; an unimplemented kind fails at render time naming the renderer. Edits from the renderer go through issue.set and re-run the flow. \"My work\" is a flow, not a built-in view. Map: doc/design/cli-convention.md.","files":null}]}